<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="page">
  <h1>Services &amp; Pricing</h1>
  <p class="lead">All prices are in Thai Baht (THB) and exclude VAT/sales tax, which Lemon Squeezy calculates at checkout based on the buyer's country. Pay by credit/debit card or PayPal.
    Every project starts with a free discovery call and a written proposal; nothing is charged until you accept it.</p>

  <div class="plans">
    <% for (const p of plans) { %>
    <div class="plan <%= p.featured ? 'featured' : '' %>" id="plan-<%= p.key %>">
      <div class="pname"><%= p.name %></div>
      <div class="pprice"><%= p.price_label %></div>
      <div class="punit muted"><%= p.unit_label %></div>
      <ul><% for (const f of (p.features || [])) { %><li><%= f %></li><% } %></ul>
      <a href="<%= p.cta_url || '/contact' %>" class="btn <%= p.featured ? 'primary' : '' %>"><%= p.cta || 'Request a quote' %></a>
    </div>
    <% } %>
  </div>
  <p class="muted small center">Prices shown are indicative starting points; the exact figure is in your written proposal. Already a customer? <a href="/portal/login">Customer login</a></p>

  <h2>How billing works</h2>
  <h3>Projects (consulting, development, websites, integrations)</h3>
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li><b>Written proposal</b> with scope, deliverables, timeline and price. Fixed price for defined scope; hourly for open-ended consulting.</li>
    <li><b>Deposit of 50%</b> on acceptance, invoiced through a Lemon Squeezy payment link; the balance on delivery. Larger projects are split into milestones, each invoiced on acceptance of that milestone.</li>
    <li>Invoices are due within 15 days. The receipt is emailed immediately by Lemon Squeezy and can carry your company name, address and tax ID.</li>
    <li>Change requests outside the agreed scope are quoted separately before any work starts.</li>
    <li>Source code and deliverables are handed over on full payment. 30-day defect-fix warranty after delivery.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Pay-as-you-go automation tools</h3>
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li><b>Free account, no card on file.</b> Unit prices per record (for example per document downloaded or per application processed) are agreed in your proposal and shown in your customer portal.</li>
    <li><b>Invoice on the 1st of every month</b> for the records actually processed in the previous month, payable within 15 days via the payment link in the portal.</li>
    <li>You can verify usage before paying: the portal lists every job, per task type and per machine, and you can export it to CSV.</li>
    <li>Jobs cancelled or interrupted midway are billed only for the records completed. Months with usage below ฿17 are carried forward (payment-provider minimum).</li>
    <li>No contract: stop using the tool and there is no further invoice. See the <a href="/refund">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Maintenance &amp; support plans</h3>
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li>Monthly plans covering hosting, monitoring, updates and a response-time commitment, invoiced monthly in advance and cancellable with 30 days' notice.</li>
    <li>Price changes for any recurring service are announced by email at least 30 days in advance.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
